From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0000
Subject: media: cedrus: refuse interlaced quarter sample MPEG-4

In interlaced quarter sample VOLs, the engine derives the chroma
vectors of field predicted macroblocks as x = r(x / 2), y = r(y) >> 1,
with r(v) = (v >> 1) | (v & 1). The ISO/IEC 14496-5 reference decoder
and FFmpeg both use y = r(y >> 1): they agree on all 40 frames of
a1ge2_asp_L4, while the engine is off in 2455 chroma macroblocks of
the first 3 frames alone. None of the FLD_QM modes, with or without
FLD_HM, gives the standard rounding.

Refuse such VOLs in the control check, so that userspace falls back to
software decoding as it does for data partitioning. Interlaced half
sample and progressive quarter sample VOLs are not affected. Field
direct mode in interlaced B-VOPs is correct: the engine matches the
reference decoder there, and FFmpeg is the one off.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
@@ -239,6 +239,16 @@
 		if (vol->flags & V4L2_MPEG4_VOL_FLAG_DATA_PARTITIONED)
 			return -EINVAL;
 
+		/*
+		 * In interlaced quarter sample VOLs, the engine derives the
+		 * chroma vectors of field predictions with another rounding
+		 * than ISO/IEC 14496-2 (its reference decoder and FFmpeg
+		 * agree), and no FLD_QM/FLD_HM mode gives the standard one.
+		 */
+		if ((vol->flags & V4L2_MPEG4_VOL_FLAG_INTERLACED) &&
+		    (vol->flags & V4L2_MPEG4_VOL_FLAG_QUARTER_SAMPLE))
+			return -EINVAL;
+
 		if (vol->video_object_layer_width > CEDRUS_MPEG4_MAX_WIDTH ||
 		    cedrus_check_pic_size(ctx, vol->video_object_layer_width,
 					  vol->video_object_layer_height))
